// §14 entry 21 -- `@transitus` bit widths not summing to a whole byte ->
// EXS-E0322.
//
// §5.2 "Bit-width fields", rule 4: "Declared widths must sum to a whole
// number of bytes. A partial trailing byte is implicit padding --
// EXS-E0322, the rule above, applied at bit granularity." `versio` (4 bits)
// and `genus` (3 bits) below sum to 7 bits, not 8 -- one bit short of a
// whole byte, so it is the same disclosure-class violation entry 7 raises
// at byte granularity, raised here at bit granularity instead. (Contrast
// §5.2's own `DeModFrame`, where `versio: u4` and `genus: u4` sum to
// exactly 8.)
//
// RUNS: the @transitus bit-width layout checker (wire-codec branch) now
// rejects this. compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are no longer empty; `exsc
// aedifica --hospes x86_64-linux --diagnostica json`, run directly against
// this file, exits 1 and emits exactly one diagnostic -- {"code":
// "EXS-E0322",...,"message":"implicit padding in a @transitus type",...} --
// confirmed, not assumed. (The code is the same E0322 as entry 7's,
// per §5.2 rule 4 applied at bit rather than byte granularity, as this
// entry's own text above already says.)

@transitus
publica structura Malum {
    versio: u4
    genus:  u3
}

// TEST: entry=21 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0322 status=run
